<title>INDIA: India produces 193.20 kg gold in February.</title>
<headline>India produces 193.20 kg gold in February.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 193.20 kg of gold in February 1997 against a target of 166.57 kg, a government statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The country produced 1,870.68 kg of gold between April 1996 and February 1997 compared with 1,469.40 kg in the same period previous year, the statement said.</p>
<p>	 February 1997	     Cumulative production</p>
<p>	    ----------		 ----------------------</p>
<p>		Actual		   Apr96-Feb97 Apr95-Feb96</p>
<p> BGML	 60.36			 622.52	580.35</p>
<p> HGML	132.84		     1,248.16	889.05</p>
<p> Total     193.20		     1,870.68    1,469.40</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in kg and provisional.</p>
<p>	    BGML: Bharat Gold Mines Limited.</p>
<p>	    HGML: Hutti Gold Mines Limited.</p>
</text>
